    "narrative": "LawDog enters today\u2019s slate with **Tyler Freeman** and **Taylor Ward** serving as our primary offensive anchors. **Tyler Freeman** is our standout play (71.80), benefiting significantly from an optimal #2 spot and a favorable matchup against Bennett; crucially, his efficiency is boosted by a 100% stolen base expectation against a slow-delivering pitcher, a vital metric given our league\u2019s aggressive focus on speed. **Taylor Ward** (71.46) also projects as an elite start, taking advantage of a high-ceiling matchup against Aldegheri. With **Jonathan Aranda** (65.29) rounding out the top-tier starts in a prime #3 slot against Wacha, we are leaning heavily on these high-OBP, high-upside options to carry the run production while we chase SB volume.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved balancing the middle infield spots, where **Geraldo Perdomo** (57.27) and **Masyn Winn** (57.61) narrowly edged out other options. While **Bryson Stott** (42.99) remains in the lineup, his utility is being throttled by a tough L/L matchup against Griffin, and he is teetering on the edge of the active threshold. We are monitoring **Yainer Diaz** (42.18) closely; despite his base projection, his score is severely hampered by Cease\u2019s elite 3.15 xERA, making him a marginal play that we are starting only due to positional scarcity. We remain sidelined by the injuries to **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith**, and with no production coming from the inactive **Cal Raleigh** or **Lawrence Butler**, our depth players\u2014including **Matt Chapman**, **Ryan Waldschmidt**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Luis Arraez**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Drew Gilbert**\u2014must remain ready to plug gaps should lineup volatility or injury status shift as the day progresses.",
